From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrummingBird1 <1979036+DrummingBird1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:42:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Vertex fetch: cached memory, and only the attributes a
 program reads

A heavy frame writes a million 256-byte vertices one component at a time into
the write-combined upload heap, the worst case for it, and that held the RSX
thread back while the GPU sat at 20 percent. The buffer moves to a WRITE_BACK
custom heap in L0 (VPVB_UPLOAD=1 goes back), and rsx_fetch_vertex resolves each
array once per draw and skips attributes rsx_vp_analyze_inputs says the program
never reads.

Sonic the Hedgehog's e0031 goes from 15-18 to 23-30 fps. VTX_FETCH_CHECK=1
compares against rsx_fetch_attrib: 430 million vertices, no difference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
